[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3977549454","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107052#issuecomment-3977549454","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107052","id":3977549454,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tFJaO","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-28T18:33:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-28T18:33:38Z","body":"Just came across this because it's similar to what I wanted to implement.\r\n\r\nI'm unsure about setting the slider lower bound to 20 Hz, even if a lower number can be typed in. It may not be clear that a lower number is acceptable, and the filter may introduce noticeable changes if the cutoff is at 20 Hz. I believe that's one of the reasons why they go from 1 Hz to 20500 Hz.\r\n\r\nAlso, I haven't tested this yet, but is an exponential slider what is needed here? Wouldn't it be a logarithmic one, since that's how a frequency spectrum is often visualized?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3977549454/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979880718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107052#issuecomment-3979880718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107052","id":3979880718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tOCkO","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T12:36:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T12:36:21Z","body":"> is an exponential slider what is needed here? Wouldn't it be a logarithmic one, since that's how a frequency spectrum is often visualized?\r\n\r\nFrequency increases exponentially as pitch increases linearly. Because humans perceive pitch linearly, it's helpful to have frequency sliders be exponential.  Check out the following (ranges capped from 20Hz to 20.5kHz):\r\n\r\nExp:\r\n![exp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b70d6ec6-83f2-427e-a04f-f2f78e4ca5bf)\r\n\r\nLog (rapidly moves into extremely high frequencies):\r\n![log](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9765bc5-de9d-49a6-9f94-521a73ae7c63)\r\n\r\nLinear (current state) (most of the slider range is spent on very high frequencies):\r\n![lin](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11214370-7adb-4f22-9d7e-444e2cfdfdca)\r\n\r\n> I'm unsure about setting the slider lower bound to 20 Hz, even if a lower number can be typed in.\r\n\r\nIf the slider itself can drag down to 1Hz while exponential, it severely offsets the usable range of the slider, where approximately half of the range is <120Hz:\r\n![exp-1hz](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d08980d2-9b6b-4906-bd33-f216a0d15517)\r\n\r\nIf someone desires a cutoff that low I'm not sure why they'd not just manually enter it. Normally if a user is using a slider instead of entering values, they're likely doing so because they're paying attention to the effect in search of a desired feel, not because they're searching for a specific number. I imagine that virtually all of the time, in the case of filters, that \"desired feel\" is going to exist well above the 20Hz range.\r\n\r\n> It may not be clear that a lower number is acceptable\r\n\r\nPerhaps it could be good to include a note about this in the docs. I can add that.\r\n\r\n> the filter may introduce noticeable changes if the cutoff is at 20 Hz\r\n\r\nCould you clarify what you mean? If you are talking about breaking compatibility, the filters can still be set down to 1Hz, so nothing would change on existing projects.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979880718/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979953376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107052#issuecomment-3979953376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107052","id":3979953376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tOUTg","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T13:25:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T13:25:12Z","body":"I see, I must've misunderstood something. Sliders look good. Though this problem is present in more than just this `AudioEffect`. Others have the same issue. Just so I know if I should work on the others or not, do you plan on fixing the other sliders as well? I think every `AudioEffect` with a cutoff option in Hz has the same problem.\r\n\r\n> Could you clarify what you mean? If you are talking about breaking compatibility, the filters can still be set down to 1Hz, so nothing would change on existing projects.\r\n\r\nIt's not about compatibility. I don't know exactly the math and code behind filters, but my worry was related to slope and phase rotation. But since it's hard for any sound around 20 Hz to be relevant, I think you can ignore me on this.\r\n\r\nLooks good :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979953376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991361185","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107052#issuecomment-3991361185","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107052","id":3991361185,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t51ah","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T14:14:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T14:14:08Z","body":"> Though this problem is present in more than just this AudioEffect. Others have the same issue. Just so I know if I should work on the others or not, do you plan on fixing the other sliders as well?\r\n\r\nThis fixes the slider for this AudioEffect as well as all the filter effects that inherit from this effect:\r\n<img width=\"222\" height=\"171\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b21ebd3b-9b1c-4dd5-978c-181ae1531f4c\" />\r\n\r\nI currently don't have any plans to change this on other effects, partially because I am not aware of other audio effects that have this frequency slider issue.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991361185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991477731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107052#issuecomment-3991477731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107052","id":3991477731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t6R3j","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T14:33:04Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T14:33:04Z","body":"Updated the docs to indicate that sub-20Hz frequencies can be set and force-pushed, got a merge conflict- turns out that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199 takes care of that already :) Rebased before pushing but I guess my fork wasn't as up-to-date as I had thought.","a